# P7 patch sketch — burst-scoped SLRU + verify-prefix retention
#
# NOT APPLIED. Sketch against src/glm53_generate.cu @ current working tree
# (branch glm53-dflash2-4070ti-super). Apply with: patch -p1 <
# scratch/host-tier/p7-slru-prefix.patch (from repo root) after review.
#
# Policy (see p7-host-tier-analysis.md):
#   1. Soft segment-LRU ("burst door"): every fresh insert waits in a
#      probation segment; only a completed-resident HIT promotes a record
#      into the protected segment. take_window() evicts probation-LRU first
#      and touches protected only when probation runs dry. One-shot
#      verify-union records (draft-tail, never re-referenced) die in
#      probation; the per-layer hot set accumulates in protected with a
#      retention horizon set by promotion rate, not burst rate.
#   2. Verify-prefix retention cap: in batch verify, admit only the first
#      VERIFY_RETAIN_POS positions' picks per layer (position 0 is
#      guaranteed accepted: main()'s truth0 pre-check already gated the
#      round; positions beyond the acceptance EMA are likely-rejected
#      draft tail).
#
# Determinism: admission/retention only decides WHICH windows stay
# resident. Every union record is still read, uploaded, and GEMV'd exactly
# once per round in the same `distinct` first-seen order with the same
# users/out_ids/combine lists, so the routed-sum FP order and the kernel
# sequence are bit-identical by construction. Payloads are byte-identical
# (byte-verified store, deterministic AVX2 expansion), so a hit vs miss
# re-read cannot change logits. Still gated by the parity A/B below.
#
# Escape hatches: INSIGNIA_GLM53_TIER_SEGMENTS=0 restores plain LRU;
# INSIGNIA_GLM53_VERIFY_RETAIN_POS=0 (default) keeps the current
# retain-everything behavior.

